<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  slidecraft-mcp-path.wxs — WiX 3 fragment merged into the MSI (bundle.windows.wix.fragmentPaths +
  componentRefs in tauri.bundle.conf.json). The MSI counterpart of windows/slidecraft-mcp-path.nsh.

  WHY: put the install dir (where slidecraft-mcp.cmd, node.exe and cli.cjs live, flat under INSTALLDIR)
  on the USER PATH, so an upstream agent registers the bundled MCP server with ONE word, like the macOS
  Homebrew cask (#519 / ADR-0022 / ADR-0038 D5). The exact `claude mcp add` command is in
  docs/mcp-server.md: it contains a double hyphen, which an XML comment must not hold (XML 1.0 §2.5;
  WiX candle.exe rejects the whole file with CNDL0104, #536), so it is not repeated here.

  How it meets the #519 invariants — all declarative, executed by Windows Installer itself:
    * USER scope: Environment/@System="no" edits the installing user's HKCU\Environment\Path, never the
      machine PATH. (Tauri's MSI is InstallScope=perMachine and elevates, but the user environment is
      still the launching user's.) Windows Installer broadcasts WM_SETTINGCHANGE itself.
    * Reversible: @Permanent="no" → removed on uninstall; MSI also rolls it back if the install fails.
    * Idempotent: Windows Installer's Environment table de-duplicates ("set"/"last" appends only when
      the value is not already present) and merges on repair/upgrade.
    * Visible: the component is referenced from Tauri's always-installed "External" feature, and the
      change is listed in the MSI log (msiexec /l*v) under WriteEnvironmentStrings.
    * A component that writes per-user data must have an HKCU registry KeyPath (MSI/ICE38 rule); the
      value doubles as a hint for support ("where is the launcher?").

  Tauri's main.wxs defines Directory Id="INSTALLDIR" (the install dir) and puts resources + external
  binaries directly under it, so [INSTALLDIR] IS the folder containing slidecraft-mcp.cmd.
  Content-pinned by tests/mcp-launcher-win-linux.test.ts (cannot be compiled on Linux CI).
-->
<Wix xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/wix/2006/wi">
  <Fragment>
    <DirectoryRef Id="INSTALLDIR">
      <Component Id="SlidecraftMcpUserPath" Guid="*">
        <RegistryValue Root="HKCU" Key="Software\The SlideCraft Authors\SlideCraft" Name="McpLauncherDir" Type="string" Value="[INSTALLDIR]" KeyPath="yes" />
        <Environment Id="SlidecraftMcpUserPathEnv" Name="PATH" Value="[INSTALLDIR]" Action="set" Part="last" Permanent="no" System="no" />
      </Component>
    </DirectoryRef>
  </Fragment>
</Wix>
